# Scoped to docker/jaguar-toolchain.Dockerfile (BuildKit convention:
# <dockerfile-name>.dockerignore applies only to that build; classic
# (non-BuildKit) docker build ignores this file and falls back to a root
# .dockerignore if one exists -- there isn't one here, so on classic builders
# the full repo tree is still sent as context. Harmless either way (the
# builder stage only COPYs tools/jaguar-toolchain/{PIN,setup.sh}), just a
# bigger context tarball than necessary.
*
# Docker's dockerignore matcher won't resurrect a file via `!` if a parent
# directory is already excluded by `*` -- so every path segment needs its
# own negation, not just the leaf files.
!tools
!tools/jaguar-toolchain
!tools/jaguar-toolchain/PIN
!tools/jaguar-toolchain/setup.sh
